From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: ICorDebugEval over Wine Mono's agent (call, new object, new string).

ICorDebugThread::CreateEval was E_NOTIMPL, so a debugger could not evaluate an expression that calls code
(property getters, ToString, watch expressions). As in the .NET Framework, an evaluation is set up while
stopped and runs at the next Continue: CallFunction and NewObject are VM INVOKE_METHOD on the eval's thread
(stopped in managed code; breakpoints do not stop it), NewString is APPDOMAIN CREATE_STRING,
NewObjectNoConstructor TYPE CREATE_INSTANCE; it ends with EvalComplete, or EvalException with the
exception object as the result, delivered on the event thread with the process stopped again. GetResult,
IsActive, GetThread; CreateValue makes primitives and null references the debugger sets and passes.
Not done: NewArray (the agent makes only byte arrays), Abort.
---
